GUI modernization, Phase 5 (second slice): incident-scoped evidence
export with an adjustable padding window - PRD U5 ("مشاركة دليل حادثة مع
طرف آخر... حادثة محددة", sharing a specific incident's evidence with
another party) and the execution order's own Phase 5 line ("Evidence
(incident-scoped 'export this incident' with an adjustable padding
window)").

## 1. The gap

Evidence.tsx's export was always a fixed recent window (last hour/day/
week ending now) - there was no way to export evidence for one specific
incident without guessing a window wide enough to contain it and narrow
enough not to hand over the rest of the record. `desktop/src/routing/
useRoute.ts`'s `InvestigationContext` (`from`/`to`/`selection` among
other fields) has existed since Phase 3 specifically for this kind of
page-to-page handoff, documented in its own comment as "today, every
page - none of them read from this yet; that lands with each page's own
Phase 3/5 rebuild" - this is that rebuild, for Evidence.tsx.

## 2. What was built

`IncidentCard.tsx` gained an optional `onExport?: (incident: Incident)
=> void` prop and a footer "Export this incident's evidence…" button,
shown only when the prop is given - the wizard's `SampleInvestigationStep`
(demo mode, nothing to export to) correctly shows no button since it
never passes one.

`Incidents.tsx`'s new `contextForIncidentExport(incident)` (exported for
direct testing) computes the incident's own window: `opened_at` to
`closed_at`, or to the last chain link's own time for an incident that
never closed (a better proxy for "when this was actually observed" than
the export moment, which could be hours later), falling back to
`opened_at` itself only if the chain is empty too. Wires `onExport` to
`navigate("evidence", {from, to, selection: incident_id})`.

`Evidence.tsx` gained a `context: InvestigationContext` prop (from
`App.tsx`'s `route.context`, threaded the same way `record`/`settings`
already were). When `context.from`/`context.to` are both present it
shows an "Exporting evidence for this incident" card instead of the
generic one: the incident's own translated title (looked up in
`record.incidents` by `context.selection`, via the same `findRule`/
`titleFor` used everywhere else this session - falls back to showing
just the raw window if the incident is not in the current record) and
its window, a padding-in-minutes input (default 5, the
`DEFAULT_PADDING_MINUTES` constant) in place of the generic 1h/24h/7d
selector, and an export button now labelled to match ("Export this
incident's evidence…" instead of the generic "Export an evidence
bundle…" - a real inconsistency the tests below caught before this log
was written, see §4). `doExport` computes `since`/`until` as the
incident's own from/to padded by the minutes value in incident-scoped
mode, or the existing generic window math otherwise - one function, two
branches, not a second copy of the export call.

`docs/desktop.md`'s Evidence bundles section documents the new button
and its default padding.

## 3. Full regression

    $ npx tsc --noEmit                             clean
    $ npm test                                     12 files, 71 tests passed
    $ npm run build                                clean
    $ npx playwright test                          35 passed (0 failed) -
        the Latin-scanner found zero new violations from any of the new
        strings (all real translation keys, both languages)

## 4. A real bug the new tests caught before this ever reached a browser

Writing `Evidence.test.tsx`'s export-trigger test first (click the
button, assert the padded since/until reached `agentExportBundle`)
failed: the actual export button still said "Export an evidence
bundle…" in incident-scoped mode, because the button's own label was
never switched when the surrounding card was - an oversight in the
first pass at this feature, not a pre-existing bug. Fixed the component
(the button now reads "Export this incident's evidence…" specifically
in scoped mode) rather than the test, and the padding-math tests
(exact `since`/`until` for the default 5-minute padding and for an
adjusted 10-minute value, both against a fixed incident window so the
expected timestamps are exact literals, not "approximately right")
then passed against the real component. This is exactly why the
padding math got a real interaction test instead of only a rendering
check - a bug here would otherwise have shipped invisibly (the page
would still "look right" with the wrong button reachable).

## 5. Actually looked at it

Fresh browser tab, demo recording, Arabic then a sidebar-navigated check
in the same session:
- Clicked "تصدير أدلة هذه الحادثة…" (Export this incident's evidence…)
  on the first incident on the Incidents page - landed on the Evidence
  page showing "تصدير أدلة هذه الحادثة" (the scoped title), the
  incident's own translated title with its id in `TechnicalValue`
  ("تعطّلت وصلة وسحبت معها أجهزة أخرى (01M2E02JGAFE9JP3A3D49T45P5)"),
  and its computed window ("٢٢:٢١:٢٥ → ٢٢:٢٢:٠٥"). Demo mode correctly
  shows "التصدير متاح عند الاتصال بالراصد الحي" (export needs a live
  recorder) instead of padding/export controls that could not do
  anything - the same honest gating the generic export path already
  had, applied consistently to the new one.
- Navigated back to Evidence via the sidebar (no routing context):
  confirmed the original generic mode is completely unchanged - "تصدير
  هذا التسجيل" (Export this recording), the 44-event/16-incident counts,
  the 1h/24h/7d selector all still there exactly as before this slice.
- Console clean throughout.

## 6. Not verifiable in this environment

The actual bundle export call (`agentExportBundle`) only runs against a
live recorder connection, which this sandbox has none of - covered
instead by the mocked `Evidence.test.tsx` tests, which capture the exact
query string a real export would send and assert the since/until values
precisely (not merely that some value was sent). This is the same
honestly-scoped verification pattern used for the Rust/Go structured
error codes in evidence 39.

## 7. What remains in Phase 5

Incidents master/detail with search/sort/filter; Rules bilingual
catalogue improvements; Settings regrouped into six sections with a
sticky save/discard bar and unsaved-changes guard; Diagnostics'
secret-free support-summary copy button with a preview. No new ADR here
either - this extends the existing bundle/API contract with a client-
side computation over the same `/v1/bundle?since&until` parameters that
already existed, not a new field or endpoint.
